1
00:00:00,824 --> 00:00:01,801
A shared phone.

2
00:00:01,858 --> 00:00:03,892
Twenty minutes, three days a week.

3
00:00:03,949 --> 00:00:06,344
No tutor, no reliable internet.

4
00:00:06,413 --> 00:00:08,989
This is Maya — and there are millions like her.

5
00:00:14,648 --> 00:00:16,375
Bright students in underserved schools

6
00:00:16,415 --> 00:00:19,339
don't lack free material — they lack follow-through.

7
00:00:19,408 --> 00:00:22,861
Practice results, class notes, occasional tutoring:

8
00:00:22,893 --> 00:00:26,178
all fragmented. Every session starts from zero.

9
00:00:30,536 --> 00:00:32,282
A chatbot answers questions.

10
00:00:32,339 --> 00:00:33,713
An agent takes action.

11
00:00:33,769 --> 00:00:38,465
GitLearnOS turns one learner-owned Git repository into durable state —

12
00:00:38,505 --> 00:00:41,770
so any AI agent becomes a tutor that never forgets,

13
00:00:41,810 --> 00:00:43,148
and never locks you in.

14
00:00:48,436 --> 00:00:51,048
Real practice becomes an evidence-linked gap.

15
00:00:51,104 --> 00:00:54,305
The agent picks the smallest useful next question —

16
00:00:54,338 --> 00:00:55,555
not another worksheet.

17
00:00:55,612 --> 00:00:57,290
Every answer is preserved,

18
00:00:57,330 --> 00:00:59,858
every step is a reversible Git commit.

19
00:00:59,914 --> 00:01:02,478
Auditable. Undoable. Yours.

20
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:09,843
Here is a real SAT workflow.

21
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:13,845
Maya imports feedback from Bluebook Reading and Writing Module One:

22
00:01:13,974 --> 00:01:17,800
two Words in Context misses, both chosen by topic match.

23
00:01:17,856 --> 00:01:21,802
The agent preserves that evidence without inventing a score trend.

24
00:01:21,859 --> 00:01:23,970
It asks for the meaning before the choices,

25
00:01:24,010 --> 00:01:26,826
then gives one original SAT-style item.

26
00:01:26,883 --> 00:01:30,143
Maya explains her reasoning and answers without a hint.

27
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:33,833
GitLearnOS saves the reasoning, not just the letter,

28
00:01:33,842 --> 00:01:35,937
turns it into a reusable rule,

29
00:01:35,993 --> 00:01:39,014
and queues a new passage for forty-eight hours later.

30
00:01:39,082 --> 00:01:41,297
One immediate success stays learning.

31
00:01:41,354 --> 00:01:43,052
Transfer is the evidence.

32
00:01:53,236 --> 00:01:57,603
Text-first. No database, no server, nothing always-on.

33
00:01:57,659 --> 00:02:00,547
It works with the free materials schools already have,

34
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:02,836
and with any agent the student can reach —

35
00:02:02,876 --> 00:02:07,362
ChatGPT, Claude, Codex, OpenCode — or none at all.

36
00:02:07,419 --> 00:02:09,393
The learner owns every byte.

37
00:02:15,836 --> 00:02:16,981
GitLearnOS.

38
00:02:17,038 --> 00:02:20,118
Learning happens anywhere — the state belongs to you.

